Yeah Hand (formerly Rebelia) - License Overview
================================================

This repository contains different kinds of content, each released under its
own open license. The full license texts are in the respective folders.

Hardware
========
SPDX-License-Identifier: CERN-OHL-S-2.0

The hardware design (CAD models, STL files, electronic board design files,
Gerber files, netlists and part lists in /hardware) is released under the
CERN Open Hardware Licence Version 2 - Strongly Reciprocal (CERN-OHL-S v2).
Full text: hardware/LICENSE.txt - https://ohwr.org/cern_ohl_s_v2.txt

Source location: https://github.com/opsobot/rebelia

Firmware
========
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later

The firmware (source code for the ESP32-based board in /firmware) is released
under the GNU General Public License, version 3 or (at your option) any later
version.
Full text: firmware/LICENSE.txt - https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.html

Documentation, pictures and renders
===================================
SPDX-License-Identifier: CC-BY-SA-4.0

Documentation (/docs), pictures, renders and other multimedia content are
released under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International
License.
Full text: hardware/renders/LICENSE.txt - https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/legalcode

Patents
=======
Both CERN-OHL-S v2 and GPLv3 include an express patent licence from every
licensor and contributor, covering the patents necessary to use their
contributions. See VARIANTS.md and docs/defensive-publication/ for the public
technical disclosure of this design.

Trademark
=========
The licenses above do not grant any right to use the "Yeah Hand" name,
which is a registered EU trademark (no. 019374244). See TRADEMARK.md.

